      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}) \\\\  & =2y{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}+2{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}+2y} \\\\  & =2y(y+1){e}^{{x}^{2}+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
